Superstore Sales Analysis: Data Storytelling & Statistical Validation
Executive Summary

This project analyzes the Superstore sales dataset to identify key business trends, customer behavior, product performance, and profitability. Using Python libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn, the dataset was cleaned, explored, and visualized to generate meaningful business insights. Statistical hypothesis testing was also performed to validate whether the average profit of the Technology category differs significantly from the Furniture category. The findings provide data-driven recommendations that can help improve business performance and support better decision-making.
Project Objective
The main objective of this project is to analyze the Superstore sales data and identify important business insights related to sales, profit, customers, regions, product categories, and shipping methods. The project also validates business findings using statistical hypothesis testing.
Business Problem
The Superstore operates across multiple regions, customer segments, and product categories. Management requires insights to answer the following questions:

Which region generates the highest sales?
Which product category earns the highest profit?
Which customer segment contributes the most revenue?
Which products perform the best?
How do discounts affect profitability?
Is there a statistically significant difference in profit between Technology and Furniture products?

This project aims to answer these questions through data analysis and statistical validation.

